1
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:07,695
Now I've taken weakness as my ally

2
00:00:07,696 --> 00:00:11,347
I can fly to the highest heights

3
00:00:11,347 --> 00:00:14,130
If I would just stop here

4
00:00:14,130 --> 00:00:18,782
all I've lost would lose its luster

5
00:00:18,782 --> 00:00:22,304
If you were lost out somewhere

6
00:00:22,304 --> 00:00:25,912
at the same time my heart is shaken

7
00:00:25,913 --> 00:00:28,782
Id have no way to find you

8
00:00:28,782 --> 00:00:32,826
your kindness, or even your strength

9
00:00:32,826 --> 00:00:38,521
I know

10
00:00:38,521 --> 00:00:40,391
It's time for the dawn!

11
00:00:40,478 --> 00:00:43,782
My peak performance

12
00:00:43,869 --> 00:00:47,826
I'll blow straight past in a blast, yeah

13
00:00:47,826 --> 00:00:50,608
You'll be left frozen with laughs

14
00:00:50,608 --> 00:00:55,043
The days of pain left in the past, let's hope

15
00:00:55,043 --> 00:00:57,869
As I make foes of the world

16
00:00:57,869 --> 00:01:02,304
I'm bracing myself upon shaking legs, yeah

17
00:01:02,304 --> 00:01:05,043
Just keep me going for a few more steps

18
00:01:05,043 --> 00:01:09,912
Now, this is the comeback, the time to awaken is now

19
00:01:19,521 --> 00:01:24,478
Now, this is the comeback, the time to awaken is now

20
00:01:34,957 --> 00:01:38,174
Winding our story's clock back
just a little bit...

21
00:01:39,696 --> 00:01:44,217
Here we find what once was the final resting place of
Kozuki Oden and his retainers, including Kin'emon:

22
00:01:44,217 --> 00:01:46,391
The ruins of Oden Castle, in Kuri.

23
00:02:04,608 --> 00:02:10,478
Kaido's Blast Breath left nothing
of the ruins in its wake.

24
00:02:11,782 --> 00:02:16,521
It was there that Oden constructed
his first castle upon becoming Daimyo of Kuri.

25
00:02:17,391 --> 00:02:20,652
Daimyo!

26
00:02:22,913 --> 00:02:24,913
Luffy!

27
00:02:25,435 --> 00:02:27,304
Hey there!

28
00:02:27,304 --> 00:02:29,043
Luffytaro-san!

29
00:02:29,043 --> 00:02:32,216
Yo! What's got the
whole gang comin' here?

30
00:02:32,217 --> 00:02:35,347
We have come to tell
Oden-sama of our victory.

31
00:02:35,347 --> 00:02:38,956
There are other matters we want
to discuss with him as well.

32
00:02:38,957 --> 00:02:41,652
Why's you-gara here, though?

33
00:02:41,652 --> 00:02:43,609
I'm here to see Oden!

34
00:02:48,304 --> 00:02:54,130
I am certain Oden-sama is overjoyed
to meet with the Savior of Wano!

35
00:02:54,130 --> 00:02:55,521
Ya really think so?

36
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,521
Oden-sama...

37
00:02:59,521 --> 00:03:04,043
It is thanks to Luffytaro-dono and the others here
that we were able to fell Orochi and Kaido,

38
00:03:04,043 --> 00:03:06,782
and return the Land of Wano
to her people.

39
00:03:18,782 --> 00:03:22,956
We, together with our new Shogun,
Momonosuke-sama,

40
00:03:22,957 --> 00:03:27,565
swear to you that we shall restore
our country to what it once was,

41
00:03:27,608 --> 00:03:29,217
a place where all can live in peace.

42
00:03:34,435 --> 00:03:37,695
How I wish Ashura and Izo
could join us here...

43
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:52,826
They are here.

44
00:03:53,217 --> 00:03:57,739
Within our bosoms,
alongside Oden-sama.

45
00:03:57,739 --> 00:04:00,130
Mmm, true that.

46
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:04,086
Certainly they must be hosting
a grand feast in the afterlife!

47
00:04:04,086 --> 00:04:05,956
Prrrmeow meowmeow!

48
00:04:05,957 --> 00:04:10,522
Oden cooked by Oden-sama
was the most delicious thing in the world!

49
00:04:11,957 --> 00:04:16,652
Ah, yes... I do recall its taste,
and how we all used to share in it.

50
00:04:16,652 --> 00:04:21,391
Aye. It tasted even better
after training with Oden-sama.

51
00:04:21,478 --> 00:04:24,826
Sounds neat!
Wish I coulda had some!

52
00:04:24,826 --> 00:04:26,434
Me, too!

53
00:04:26,435 --> 00:04:29,608
Let's ask Sanji-kun
to cook it for us sometime!

54
00:04:30,696 --> 00:04:33,782
We ought to stock up on
ingredients for it then!

55
00:04:33,869 --> 00:04:37,826
Totally! We're gonna buy tons!

56
00:04:37,826 --> 00:04:39,130
Luffy-dono...

57
00:04:40,260 --> 00:04:41,477
Are you departing?

58
00:04:42,957 --> 00:04:43,913
Yeah.

59
00:04:45,347 --> 00:04:48,608
We would like to take this opportunity...

60
00:04:48,608 --> 00:04:52,130
...to once again offer
our most sincere gratitude!

61
00:04:52,217 --> 00:04:53,521
Whoooa?!

62
00:04:56,043 --> 00:04:58,999
C'mon, cut that out!
We're friends, ain't we?

63
00:05:01,304 --> 00:05:03,173
Luffy!

64
00:05:06,739 --> 00:05:07,869
Carrot!

65
00:05:07,869 --> 00:05:11,695
You're leaving already?
You can't, you can't, you just can't!

66
00:05:14,957 --> 00:05:18,347
I don't wanna say goodbye to Nami, either!
Dun wanna, dun wanna, I dun wanna!

67
00:05:18,347 --> 00:05:19,477
Carrot...

68
00:05:19,478 --> 00:05:21,174
Hey, what's botherin' ya?

69
00:05:21,826 --> 00:05:23,521
We're going back home...

70
00:05:23,521 --> 00:05:25,608
...to the Mokomo Dukedom!

71
00:05:25,608 --> 00:05:29,347
I'm gonna be defending our home
along with Wanda and everyone else!

72
00:05:33,608 --> 00:05:35,347
Miyagi, Tristan...
2112

73
00:05:35,739 --> 00:05:37,391
Thank you both!

74
00:05:37,391 --> 00:05:42,826
Thank you for all
you've taught me about medicine!

75
00:05:42,826 --> 00:05:45,304
Dr. Chopper, take care of yourself!

76
00:05:46,608 --> 00:05:48,738
If I do recall, Carrot-san,

77
00:05:48,739 --> 00:05:54,130
you stowed away aboard the Sunny
because you wanted to see the sea, no?

78
00:05:54,130 --> 00:05:55,565
Well, how'd you like it?

79
00:05:55,565 --> 00:05:57,521
It was only the best adventure ever!

80
00:05:57,608 --> 00:06:01,651
I got to see islands I never knew existed,
and met some nice people!

81
00:06:01,652 --> 00:06:07,174
There were lotsa scary moments,
but I feel I'm a little stronger than I used to be.

82
00:06:07,217 --> 00:06:09,695
That's why the adventure
I had with you all...

83
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,435
...is something I'll treasure
for the rest of my life!

84
00:06:17,608 --> 00:06:19,608
Lemme have one last garchu
for the road!

85
00:06:19,608 --> 00:06:21,173
Garchu!

86
00:06:21,174 --> 00:06:25,347
It was super fun chatting and having a blast
with you in the women's quarters, Nami!

87
00:06:25,347 --> 00:06:27,738
Yeah, it was the best!

88
00:06:27,739 --> 00:06:29,261
You too, Chobro!

89
00:06:29,869 --> 00:06:31,391
That tickles!

90
00:06:31,478 --> 00:06:33,391
I'm happy too, Carrot!

91
00:06:33,435 --> 00:06:35,174
Garchu!

92
00:06:35,869 --> 00:06:37,434
Garchu!

93
00:06:38,217 --> 00:06:41,695
Oh, yeah! I saw Zoro on my way here.
m

94
00:06:41,696 --> 00:06:42,826
Zoro, ya say?

95
00:07:23,826 --> 00:07:25,652
Go on, it's on me.

96
00:07:38,478 --> 00:07:40,435
Whatcha doin'?

97
00:07:40,435 --> 00:07:42,435
Thought I'd share a round with him.

98
00:07:44,435 --> 00:07:46,130
I'll pour it for ya!

99
00:07:46,782 --> 00:07:50,086
You the one that left the flowers?

100
00:07:50,086 --> 00:07:51,825
Eh? Yup!

101
00:07:52,608 --> 00:07:54,608
Big Sis helped me.

102
00:07:56,826 --> 00:08:00,217
Ah, here you are, Zorojuro-san.

103
00:08:00,217 --> 00:08:01,174
Yeah.

104
00:08:24,869 --> 00:08:27,347
May you both rest in peace.

105
00:08:27,347 --> 00:08:33,390
Once they finish that big, nice temple,
I'll come to see you every day, Daddy!

106
00:08:33,391 --> 00:08:36,043
That way, you won't be lonely, right?

107
00:08:36,043 --> 00:08:37,260
Right, right?

108
00:08:46,478 --> 00:08:52,260
Your being here means the time has come
for you to depart, does it not?

109
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:53,173
Yeah.

110
00:08:54,478 --> 00:08:56,130
It shall be lonely without you.

111
00:09:03,086 --> 00:09:07,564
I shall have to bid farewell
to my father's beloved Enma, then?

112
00:09:09,435 --> 00:09:10,521
Guess so.

113
00:09:17,174 --> 00:09:18,217
I ain't givin' it back.

114
00:09:19,521 --> 00:09:21,173
Aye, of course not!

115
00:09:21,696 --> 00:09:25,913
"Enma, able to rend even
the deepest depths of hell", huh?

116
00:09:28,782 --> 00:09:30,869
Oden must've been
one helluva guy...

117
00:09:32,043 --> 00:09:35,303
'Cause he'd completely
tamed this thing, hadn't he?

118
00:09:36,086 --> 00:09:41,390
Yet you, Zorojuro-san,
liberated our nation...

119
00:09:41,391 --> 00:09:44,000
.... through your
skillful wielding of Enma.

120
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,957
Nah, not skilled enough.

121
00:09:47,478 --> 00:09:51,652
To me, it looks as if Enma is rejoicing...

122
00:09:51,652 --> 00:09:53,913
...at having found its new master.

123
00:09:58,217 --> 00:10:01,869
I... will become stronger.

124
00:10:08,913 --> 00:10:10,826
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

125
00:10:10,826 --> 00:10:14,086
The hell's this, Fraguy?!

126
00:10:14,521 --> 00:10:18,043
Yo, boss! Somethin' outta place?

127
00:10:18,043 --> 00:10:19,999
Damn right, there is!

128
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:23,130
Huuuh?! Ain't no way there is!

129
00:10:23,130 --> 00:10:24,695
Damn moron!

130
00:10:25,043 --> 00:10:29,564
Ya asked me to check out
where ya made repairs,

131
00:10:29,565 --> 00:10:33,695
and I was doin' just that, numbskull!

132
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:38,043
It's per-fect-ion,
ya ingrate!

133
00:10:39,260 --> 00:10:43,347
You coulda left me
at least one spot t'fix,

134
00:10:43,347 --> 00:10:45,304
ya absolute buffoon!

135
00:10:45,652 --> 00:10:48,260
Oh, excuse me for lettin' ya down!

136
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:50,608
So she's all repaired
and in tip-top shape?

137
00:10:50,608 --> 00:10:53,999
He's definitely the
Straw Hats' shipwright!

138
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,261
Later, ya total dunce!

139
00:10:58,478 --> 00:11:01,391
And stay healthy,
ya blitherin' idiot!

140
00:11:01,391 --> 00:11:03,130
What're ya yappin' about?!

141
00:11:06,652 --> 00:11:08,826
Heeey, done yet?

142
00:11:08,826 --> 00:11:12,217
Yes, sir! Yes, yes!
I'm on my way, sir!

143
00:11:12,696 --> 00:11:14,956
Right, sorry to have kept you waiting!

144
00:11:14,957 --> 00:11:15,870
No prob.

145
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:18,477
How do you feel about this?

146
00:11:18,478 --> 00:11:18,913
Eh?

147
00:11:18,913 --> 00:11:20,478
I think it's a great fit for you, sir!

148
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,869
Usohachi-san, you're cool!

149
00:11:22,869 --> 00:11:25,173
It's the most handsome
man in all of Wano!

150
00:11:25,174 --> 00:11:27,478
Look this way!

151
00:11:27,478 --> 00:11:30,478
Need something from me, m'lady?

152
00:11:31,608 --> 00:11:33,347
I love it!

153
00:11:33,347 --> 00:11:35,086
Whoa, uh, I mean,
not really...

154
00:11:35,086 --> 00:11:39,260
Oh, say no more!
I hear you, I hear you...

155
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:41,390
This color would look good on you, too!

156
00:11:41,391 --> 00:11:42,000
Neh?

157
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,696
Usohachi-san!

158
00:11:43,696 --> 00:11:45,130
Hey there, ladykiller!

159
00:11:45,130 --> 00:11:47,956
The color red was just made for him!

160
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:50,217
He's sooo hot!

161
00:11:51,608 --> 00:11:53,912
Don't go fallin' in love
with me, now!

162
00:11:53,913 --> 00:11:55,652
No, absolutely not!

163
00:11:55,652 --> 00:11:56,391
Heeh?

164
00:11:56,391 --> 00:11:59,347
All I'm after is plain black cloth!

165
00:11:59,347 --> 00:12:01,347
And a crapload of it!

166
00:12:01,347 --> 00:12:05,912
Huh? Black cloth?
For what might you need so much, sir?

167
00:12:05,913 --> 00:12:08,391
Uh? Well, uh, that's, uh...

168
00:12:08,391 --> 00:12:09,826
Don't tell anyone, but...

169
00:12:13,217 --> 00:12:15,956
WhaaaaFor that?!

170
00:12:15,957 --> 00:12:19,130
I shall provide you with
the finest available!

171
00:12:19,130 --> 00:12:21,087
Right on!
Countin' on you!

172
00:12:29,957 --> 00:12:31,043
Right, then!

173
00:12:31,043 --> 00:12:32,999
That's it for today!

174
00:12:35,304 --> 00:12:37,086
Thank you for the lesson.

175
00:12:37,086 --> 00:12:40,912
Sangoro's Specialty Soba!

176
00:12:40,913 --> 00:12:42,086
It's so good!

177
00:12:42,086 --> 00:12:44,303
I love your Specialty Soba!

178
00:12:44,304 --> 00:12:45,695
Thank you for the meal.

179
00:12:45,696 --> 00:12:46,782
Come again!

180
00:12:47,652 --> 00:12:48,956
How's it taste?

181
00:12:48,957 --> 00:12:50,521
It is the best I've ever had!

182
00:12:50,521 --> 00:12:51,956
Good to hear.

183
00:12:53,478 --> 00:12:54,869
Oh, Chuji!

184
00:12:54,869 --> 00:12:58,173
How're ya doin', little guy?

185
00:12:59,304 --> 00:13:01,217
Coochie coochie...

186
00:13:05,565 --> 00:13:06,869
Something the matter?

187
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:08,347
Oh? Oh, nothing...

188
00:13:08,869 --> 00:13:10,043
Come to think of it...

189
00:13:10,086 --> 00:13:15,825
I have yet to properly express my thanks
to you for saving me at Onigashima.

190
00:13:15,826 --> 00:13:19,695
Don't mention it!
Just doing the right thing.

191
00:13:23,565 --> 00:13:26,521
Ah, will you be coming back here again?

192
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:34,652
Because eating your soba, Sangoro-san, gives me
the strength to keep working hard, day after day!

193
00:13:34,652 --> 00:13:37,521
I'm happy just hearing that!

194
00:13:37,521 --> 00:13:39,565
But I've gotta set off soon.

195
00:13:40,652 --> 00:13:42,609
Sangoro-san, I...!

196
00:13:43,913 --> 00:13:45,565
Mr. Soba Chef?

197
00:13:45,608 --> 00:13:47,434
Badumbadumbadum!

198
00:13:47,435 --> 00:13:49,260
Could I trouble you for a bowl?

199
00:13:49,260 --> 00:13:53,477
Robin-chwan!
Thanks for comin' bwy!

200
00:13:53,478 --> 00:13:55,304
I'd like mine served hot, please.

201
00:13:55,304 --> 00:13:58,390
I'm on it, Robin-chwan!

202
00:13:58,391 --> 00:14:01,608
Ah, if I might have the same?

203
00:14:01,608 --> 00:14:02,695
Sure

204
00:14:13,043 --> 00:14:14,869
Great job, everyone!

205
00:14:14,869 --> 00:14:18,826
Go on, rest awhile
and have some oshiruko!

206
00:14:18,826 --> 00:14:21,782
Always appreciate
the refreshments, O-Tsuru-san!

207
00:14:21,782 --> 00:14:23,217
Let's dig in!

208
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,521
Looks good!

209
00:14:28,521 --> 00:14:31,043
It's oshiruko!

210
00:14:31,043 --> 00:14:33,216
Sorry to have kept you waiting!

211
00:14:33,652 --> 00:14:35,217
Dun worry 'bout it!

212
00:14:35,217 --> 00:14:36,956
Down the hatch!

213
00:14:37,957 --> 00:14:39,913
Yuu-uu-um!

214
00:14:44,957 --> 00:14:47,043
Nom, nom!

215
00:14:57,217 --> 00:14:58,695
Thank you for the food!

216
00:15:07,217 --> 00:15:10,174
O-Tsuru-san's oshiruko is the bestest!

217
00:15:12,130 --> 00:15:14,086
Ya think so?
Eat the mochi, too!

218
00:15:14,086 --> 00:15:15,173
Okay!

219
00:15:22,608 --> 00:15:24,782
It'sh shoguud!

220
00:15:24,782 --> 00:15:27,739
Eat 'til ya burst, Tama!

221
00:15:27,739 --> 00:15:28,696
Mmhmm!

222
00:15:36,304 --> 00:15:37,825
What's up, Tama?

223
00:15:39,304 --> 00:15:42,782
When I think about havin'
to say goodbye to you here,

224
00:15:42,782 --> 00:15:45,434
I get a lump in my throat...

225
00:15:46,391 --> 00:15:49,347
First Ace,
an' now you, Big Bro...

226
00:15:49,347 --> 00:15:55,173
All the people
I love leave me...

227
00:15:56,782 --> 00:15:57,434
Tama...

228
00:15:59,739 --> 00:16:03,217
You know that time ya gave me
that precious rice of yours?

229
00:16:04,869 --> 00:16:07,521
I ain't ever gonna forget that!

230
00:16:18,086 --> 00:16:23,608
Then I ain't gonna forget 'bout
you or yer crew, Big Bro!

231
00:16:23,608 --> 00:16:24,912
Deal!

232
00:16:24,913 --> 00:16:26,478
Kay, gotta get goin'.

233
00:16:26,478 --> 00:16:27,869
Okey dokey!

234
00:16:27,869 --> 00:16:30,043
We'll meet again, Tama!

235
00:16:49,478 --> 00:16:53,695
Big Bro, thank yoooou!

236
00:16:56,174 --> 00:16:59,174
I'mma be like you 'n Ace...

237
00:16:59,174 --> 00:17:02,521
an' get stronger, you'll see!

238
00:17:10,957 --> 00:17:14,130
And now, our story
returns to the present...

239
00:17:14,652 --> 00:17:19,174
Luffy! We're ready to set sail!

240
00:17:19,826 --> 00:17:21,130
Gotcha!

241
00:17:21,130 --> 00:17:24,434
But are you really sure
about leaving like this?

242
00:17:24,435 --> 00:17:29,217
We didn't say goodbye
to Momo-chan and Kin'emon.

243
00:17:29,217 --> 00:17:31,260
Oh yeah, you're right.

244
00:17:31,260 --> 00:17:34,173
We don't gotta go that far.

245
00:17:34,174 --> 00:17:36,347
Pretty cold, comin' outta you, Mossbrain.

246
00:17:36,347 --> 00:17:38,173
Shut it, Swirlybrow.

247
00:17:41,739 --> 00:17:48,086
But of all the people in Wano,
they shared in our adventures the most.

248
00:17:48,086 --> 00:17:51,564
Quite, it seems a bit sad
to part ways like this.

249
00:17:57,086 --> 00:17:59,608
Luffy, what do you wanna do?

250
00:18:04,869 --> 00:18:08,130
It'll be fine.
He'll come!

251
00:18:33,957 --> 00:18:36,739
"Time's up'

252
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,478
Someone said again, with a laugh

253
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:46,348
Fine then, hide-and-seek playtime...

254
00:18:47,086 --> 00:18:48,086
...is over

255
00:18:49,913 --> 00:18:53,348
Let's go, come on (We can see it soon)

256
00:18:53,478 --> 00:18:57,130
Let your heart beat out

257
00:18:58,130 --> 00:19:01,391
and things will change (We can see it soon)

258
00:19:01,521 --> 00:19:05,608
Grow strong, you have time

259
00:19:05,869 --> 00:19:06,608
Raise up that dream

260
00:19:06,826 --> 00:19:13,608
The overflowing loneliness can't sustain me alone

261
00:19:13,739 --> 00:19:17,609
We were so free in our younger days

262
00:19:17,826 --> 00:19:20,956
What a dumb dream

263
00:19:21,304 --> 00:19:22,347
...to live

264
00:19:22,478 --> 00:19:26,217
Shining a light on uncharted ways

265
00:19:26,304 --> 00:19:30,348
Get on our feet and try

266
00:19:30,391 --> 00:19:34,217
Let's see the ends of the world together

267
00:19:34,304 --> 00:19:43,478
Together, we can go and fly